# agent-orchestrator — dev-only convenience (NOT the host mechanism).
#
# On the host, secrets are files under /etc/agent-orchestrator/ loaded by the
# systemd unit via LoadCredential= (ADR-0004) — never environment variables.
# systemd materializes each one into the service's private credentials
# directory, and the code reads $CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY/<name>
# (docs/config-reference.md). The three credentials are:
#
#   app-key           GitHub App private key (C2 — signs the App JWT)
#   <provider>-key    model provider key (C5); named after model.provider,
#                     e.g. anthropic-key, openrouter-key, opencode-key
#   cloudflare-token  read-only Cloudflare token (verify.sh, types:fresh)
#
# This file exists only to run the orchestrator manually during M1
# development, outside systemd. Copy to `.env` (gitignored) if your dev runner
# reads it, and point CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY at a directory holding app-key,
# <provider>-key, and cloudflare-token. Secrets never live in this repo — keep
# them on the host only.

CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY=/etc/agent-orchestrator
